xtxbench runtime switch hook (branch xtxbench off topka-q63 c0576e3e8, commit d5454e084); apply: git apply

xtxbench runtime switch hook: GGML_HIP_RUNTIME_SWITCH_FILE (off by default) lets the graph-build-time kernel switches flip between requests

GGML_CUDA_RT_SWITCH(NAME, def) replaces the static const env reads of the kernel switches (ARGMAX_FAST, KVQ_Q8,
CONV_MUL, Q8_IDS, MOE_DOWN_REDUCE, NORM_ROUTER, INPROJ_CONV, ATTN_PREP, KVQ_FWHT, GATE_UP_Q8, MMVQ_PAIR, NORM_GATE,
GDN_CONV_AB, MMQ_EPI, MMVQ_N1_Q8_0, MMVQ_N1_ROWS, MMVQ_Q5K_BIG_ROWS, MMVQ_IQ4XS_BIG_ROWS, MMVQ_Q4K_STREAM, CONV_ROWS4,
NORM_FAST, GDN_PREFETCH). Without the env variable each site resolves once from the environment to the value of the
old static read (lossless, one relaxed atomic compare per call). With GGML_HIP_RUNTIME_SWITCH_FILE=<path> graph_compute
stats the file at most every 20 ms; a changed NAME=VALUE set bumps the switch generation, the sites re-resolve (file >
env > default), and each context synchronizes and drops its captured HIP graphs + PM4 tapes (the idle-eviction path),
so the next capture uses the new kernels. GGML_HIP_PM4 and GGML_HIP_INPUT_BATCH stay process-level.

